          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "The signed flux formula gives a useful bound with an important direction: an upper weighted-energy bound gives a lower bound on the amplitude-weighted trace. To obtain a negative Laguerre witness, we would need an upper bound on the signed modulus term or a lower bound on the bulk mass.\n\nFor the RH-to-simplicity tube remainder, the transfer retains an inverse-time cost near a double event. The exact quadratic model shows that this cost cannot be removed from a bound based only on weighted area.\n"
